  "notes": "Running\nTake about 5 minutes. Pupils choose the fair plan independently, then explain their choice to a partner. Check that they can identify what changes and what stays the same.\n\nAnswers\nA: Different water amounts; same light, plants, soil and pots.\n\nMisconceptions\nThe plan with different water and different light changes two factors, so pupils cannot tell which caused a growth difference. The plan with the same water but different light tests light, not water. Explain that only water amount should change; keep other conditions the same.\n\nBackground\nA fair test changes one factor at a time. The factor deliberately changed is the independent variable; the measured outcome here is plant growth.",
